WEBVTT

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday the fourteenth of October. Have we got everyone on?</v>

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.429
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'm here. Bit of an echo, but I can hear you.</v>

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.210
<v Sarah Okafor>Probably this room. Anyway, the broken coffee machine in the canteen has made me extremely popular this morning.</v>

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.039
<v Tomasz Nowak>It's dispensing disappointment again, is it?</v>

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:36.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Exclusively. And the heating in the portakabin seems to have two settings: off and tropical. Just having a moan, neither is going on this list.</v>

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.179
<v Marcus Hale>Tropical sounds quite nice from where I'm sitting.</v>

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get distracted completely—finished bits first.</v>

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:50.679
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, so I signed off the inspection on the 11kV Switchboard on Tuesday. That's complete.</v>

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.380
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely, closed, not rolling that forward.</v>

00:00:55.719 --> 00:01:01.670
<v Fiona Doyle>And I already swapped the filter on the chiller on three yesterday. That one's done as well.</v>

00:01:03.789 --> 00:01:11.489
<v Callum Reid>Same sort of update from me: already swapped the filter on the Water Booster Pump yesterday. Finished, not another job for today.</v>

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.030
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. Nice to hear the word finished occasionally.</v>

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:26.150
<v David Whitfield>Um, just an observation from me. I saw the pressure on the outfeed conveyor dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:28.069 --> 00:01:30.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Came back without anyone touching anything?</v>

00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:36.719
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, on its own. Not raising a job off it, just saying what I saw.</v>

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:43.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. I heard a slight rattle from the BFP, nothing to action yet. Same thing, observation only.</v>

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.329
<v Marcus Hale>Understood. Not treating that as a new maintenance request.</v>

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:56.140
<v Fiona Doyle>On the blocked stuff, still waiting on parts for the waste heat boiler, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:01.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, still blocked. Nothing new being handed out on that.</v>

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:07.640
<v Marcus Hale>And I can't get to the main water valve until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:08.659 --> 00:02:12.860
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, there isn't a window available. That's why it's still sat there.</v>

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:18.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, existing blocker, not a fresh action. Let's get onto what we can actually agree.</v>

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:25.979
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah Price, can you do the pre-use checks on the trucks? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.199
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll do the pre-use checks on the trucks.</v>

00:02:32.879 --> 00:02:36.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Important, just not an urgent one in the list.</v>

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.949
<v Hannah Price>Understood. And pre-use still means before they're used, obviously.</v>

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:46.449
<v Hannah Price>While I'm on, I'll check the guarding on the pick and place on two tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:02:47.759 --> 00:02:50.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. Tomorrow at 9:30 for that guarding check.</v>

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.810
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's the time I've got. I'll do it then.</v>

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:01.289
<v Callum Reid>I'll sort the training records for the new starters next week as well.</v>

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.449
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, you clipped slightly—next week for the records?</v>

00:03:06.889 --> 00:03:10.740
<v Callum Reid>Next week, yeah. I'll sort them. Not saying they're already done.</v>

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Got you, Callum. Training records with you, next week.</v>

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.439
<v Tomasz Nowak>There's also spare parts for the IM3. We need to order those. That still needs doing.</v>

00:03:21.759 --> 00:03:26.659
<v David Whitfield>Has that actually got an owner, or is it just sitting on the list?</v>

00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:30.849
<v Tomasz Nowak>No owner. I'm raising it, not volunteering to take it.</v>

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:35.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, ordering spare parts for the IM3 stays unallocated. Nobody's taken that.</v>

00:03:37.469 --> 00:03:43.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum, can you investigate the pressure drop on the IM1 hydraulic unit by Monday? Normal priority.</v>

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:50.340
<v Callum Reid>I can't take that one, sorry. I haven't got the capacity to give it a proper look.</v>

00:03:51.659 --> 00:03:59.009
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Fi, can I hand that to you instead—the pressure drop on the IM1 hydraulic unit, by Monday, normal priority?</v>

00:04:00.289 --> 00:04:05.889
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the IM1 hydraulic unit by Monday. Normal priority, understood.</v>

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:13.530
<v David Whitfield>Just to be clear, that's an investigation, not a promise it'll be repaired by Monday?</v>

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:20.279
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. I'll investigate it. We're not agreeing a repair off the back of a guess.</v>

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Investigation with Fi, not Callum.</v>

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:31.120
<v Marcus Hale>There's the purchase order for the turbine one gas valve as well. That needs chasing.</v>

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:39.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. Hannah Price, can you chase the purchase order for the turbine one gas valve by next Tuesday? No rush.</v>

00:04:39.709 --> 00:04:46.360
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I'll chase the purchase order for the turbine one gas valve by next Tuesday. No rush, got it.</v>

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:52.370
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers. It's the purchase order we're talking about, not doing anything to the valve.</v>

00:04:53.689 --> 00:05:01.040
<v Sarah Okafor>And Han, can you update the risk assessment for work on the fire panel today? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.790
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the fire panel today.</v>

00:05:10.069 --> 00:05:15.319
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, talking over you—just the assessment, we're not agreeing work on the panel itself here?</v>

00:05:16.319 --> 00:05:19.819
<v Hannah Price>Just the risk assessment, yeah. No physical work being added.</v>

00:05:22.079 --> 00:05:26.629
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. It matters but it's not urgent; today is still the deadline.</v>

00:05:27.019 --> 00:05:32.269
<v Callum Reid>Quite a few different dates in there. Easy to hear all that as 'everything today'.</v>

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:37.480
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, no. Risk assessment today; the other dates are as we've just agreed.</v>

00:05:39.709 --> 00:05:43.560
<v Fiona Doyle>And my investigation is Monday, normal priority. I've got that straight.</v>

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, exactly.</v>

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:53.939
<v Tomasz Nowak>And the IM3 order is still nobody's? Just checking it hasn't acquired my name because I mentioned it.</v>

00:05:55.939 --> 00:05:59.089
<v Sarah Okafor>Still nobody's. Raised as needing doing, but not allocated.</v>

00:06:00.269 --> 00:06:04.819
<v Marcus Hale>Fine. Main water valve stays blocked too, then. No access window, no change.</v>

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:10.199
<v Fiona Doyle>Same with the waste heat boiler. Still waiting on the parts; nothing moving there.</v>

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:16.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Those stay as blockers, and the completed bits stay closed. No extra actions hidden in the updates.</v>

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:23.430
<v David Whitfield>Good. It's absolutely tipping it down outside, by the way. Lovely morning for a factory.</v>

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.019
<v Callum Reid>At least we've got the tropical portakabin experience.</v>

00:06:27.589 --> 00:06:30.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Luxury, isn't it? Right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>
